{"id":"mimid-1wgh.101","title":"JMAP: jmap-chat-federation: peer discovery, auth and peer-role access","description":"In scope by decision mimid-1wgh.98 (Mark, 2026-11-22). Not planned: read the draft, face the tension below, and put a plan in this field for Mark before any code.

WHAT THE DRAFT DOES. For the topology where each participant runs their own JMAP server, exchanging messages directly.

THE TENSION, and the first question rather than an implementation detail: mimid already federates, over MIMI protocol-07 provider-to-provider with RFC 9421 signatures, PKIX and DANE client certificates (epic mimid-75nk, crates/mimid-server/src/peer.rs). This draft federates over JMAP instead. Are they complementary, serving different deployments, or two answers to one question? Write the comparison for Mark before any code, and say plainly if implementing both would mean mimid has two federation stories a reader must hold at once.","status":"open","priority":3,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mark@reviewcommit.com","created_at":"2026-11-22T22:47:06.266180142Z","created_by":"Mark Atwood","updated_at":"2026-11-22T22:47:06.266180142Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"mimid-1wgh.101","depends_on_id":"mimid-1wgh","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-11-22T22:47:06.293345277Z","created_by":"Mark Atwood","metadata":"{}"}]}
